--TEST--
A call of a value declared only `callable` checks each argument against the whole type its parameter declares, so an unrelated class, a wrong array element and a value of another enum throw `LogicError` before the body runs, while `null` reaches a `?C` parameter — `rule:types/callable-signature` and `rule:types/anonymous-function`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `Runner::run` takes a bare `callable`, so the compiler cannot check its arguments.
// `Arg` has no `mixed` in it, because a bare `callable` does not take `mixed`.
// Each body prints `body` when it runs.
enum Level: int { Low = 1, High = 7 }
// `Blue`'s value 3 is not a value of `Level`. `Red`'s value 1 is.
enum Color: int { Red = 1, Blue = 3 }
class Pet { public string $name = "pet"; }
class Rock { public int $weight = 9; }
type Arg = ?(Pet|Rock|Color|array<int|string>|string);

class Runner {
    public static function run(callable $f, Arg $v): mixed {
        return $f($v);
    }
    public static function attempt(callable $f, Arg $v): void {
        try {
            mixed $r = Runner::run($f, $v);
            echo "ran\n";
        } catch (Throwable $e) {
            echo Core\Reflect::forObject($e)->name(), ": ", $e->message, "\n";
        }
    }
}

// A class parameter, and its nullable twin, given an unrelated class.
Runner::attempt(fn (Pet $p): string => { echo "body\n"; return $p->name; }, new Rock());
Runner::attempt(fn (?Pet $p): string => { echo "body\n"; return "p"; }, new Rock());
// `null` reaches the nullable twin.
Runner::attempt(fn (?Pet $p): string => { echo "body\n"; return "p"; }, null);

// Each element of the array is checked against `int`.
array<int|string> $mixedList = [1, "two", 3];
Runner::attempt(fn (array<int> $a): uint => { echo "body\n"; return Core\Arr::count($a); }, $mixedList);

// An enum parameter is checked by the case value: two enums with one backing
// are not told apart, so `Color::Red` reaches a `Level` parameter.
Runner::attempt(fn (Level $l): int => { echo "body\n"; return $l as int; }, Color::Blue);
Runner::attempt(fn (Level $l): int => { echo "body\n"; return $l as int; }, Color::Red);

Runner::attempt(fn (?float $x): string => { echo "body\n"; return "x"; }, "text");

// A correct call runs the body and returns its value.
Runner::attempt(fn (Pet $p): string => { echo "body\n"; return $p->name; }, new Pet());
echo Runner::run(fn (Pet $p): string => $p->name, new Pet()), "\n";
--EXPECT--
LogicError: argument 1 to a `callable` does not accept an object of class `Rock`
LogicError: argument 1 to a `callable` does not accept an object of class `Rock`
body
ran
LogicError: argument 1 to a `callable` does not accept an array holding a string
LogicError: argument 1 to a `callable` does not accept an int
body
ran
LogicError: argument 1 to a `callable` does not accept a string
body
ran
pet
